      "writtenOn": "2020-12-30T09:46:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s a bit weird, I think those flags are more meant persist value across EC reboots (as is required on kukui as the EC resets everytime the AP reboots). Does this also mean that a subsequent AP non-watchdog reboot will still have the flag set?\n\nFrom https://crrev.com/c/2607204, it does appear that the \"reset: AP watchdog\" is logged in the output of `ectool --name\u003dcros_ec uptimeinfo`. What is the logic in coreboot? Should it check if the last entry is a watchdog? (instead of looking at EC reset flags?)",
      "revId": "2a08d2d9e4c36109d34d4c24b00d352044016c5f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a4fa859d_f21421e2",
        "filename": "power/mt8192.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 169,
      "author": {
        "id": 1353551
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-05T04:49:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e those flags are more meant persist value across EC reboots\n\nEC reboot with \"reboot\" will reset the flags. However, these flags are persistent with command \"reboot preserve\". Do we care about this?\n\n\u003e Does this also mean that a subsequent AP non-watchdog reboot will still have the flag set?\n\nYes, but this can be solved by adding an \u0027else\u0027 block clearing the watchdog flag.\n\n\u003e What is the logic in coreboot?\n\nIf CHROMEOS_USE_EC_WATCHDOG_FLAG is enabled, coreboot looks for EC_RESET_FLAG_AP_WATCHDOG\u003dBIT(18) in ec_reset_flags. From CL:2607204, ec_reset_flags doesn\u0027t contain this flag. The \"reset: AP watchdog\" output is from field \"recent_ap_reset[i].reset_cause\".",
      "parentUuid": "b068e0e3_2e1b4a5c",
      "revId": "2a08d2d9e4c36109d34d4c24b00d352044016c5f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a843e1c8_0a1f7f52",
        "filename": "power/mt8192.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 169,
      "author": {
        "id": 1182824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-05T06:39:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e However, these flags are persistent with command \"reboot preserve\". Do we care about this?\n\nNo. Reboot preserved is a flag for kukui only.\n\n\n\u003e If CHROMEOS_USE_EC_WATCHDOG_FLAG is enabled, coreboot looks for EC_RESET_FLAG_AP_WATCHDOG\u003dBIT(18) in ec_reset_flags. From CL:2607204, ec_reset_flags doesn\u0027t contain this flag. The \"reset: AP watchdog\" output is from field \"recent_ap_reset[i].reset_cause\".\n\nThe logic is weird. system_reset flags (i.e. ec_reset_flags) are used during a EC reset, and a AP WDT should (ideally) not trigger an EC reset unless it is needed, for example, mt8183 platforms.\n\nThe better way is checking the reset_cause of recent_ap_reset.",
      "parentUuid": "a4fa859d_f21421e2",
      "revId": "2a08d2d9e4c36109d34d4c24b00d352044016c5f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e26cd6ec_3aa4e5a0",
        "filename": "power/mt8192.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 169,
      "author": {
        "id": 1353551
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-05T07:24:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e a AP WDT should (ideally) not trigger an EC reset\n\nCurrently (even with this CL) EC reset won\u0027t be triggered, right? Do you mean we shouldn\u0027t modify ec_reset_flags on AP watchdog reset?",
      "parentUuid": "a843e1c8_0a1f7f52",
      "revId": "2a08d2d9e4c36109d34d4c24b00d352044016c5f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
